    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. His massive advantage stems from a favorable matchup against Burke, combined with a 14% boost from a dynamic platoon split and the prime lead-off spot. Following closely are **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (66.06), both of whom benefit significantly from a hitter-friendly park and a favorable matchup against Baz, whose 4.26 xERA provides a soft landing for our middle-of-the-order firepower. **Heliot Ramos** also warrants attention; despite the left-handed opponent, his 16% SP skill boost helps him outperform his raw projection, signaling a high-floor play in the five-hole.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range of the bench, specifically **Josh Jung** (46.15) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (44.74). **Josh Jung** came closest to cracking the starting nine, but his efficiency was ultimately stifled by an unhelpful matchup against Messick. We opted to prioritize the higher raw efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** and **Josh Lowe** to maintain our aggressive stance on stolen bases, despite their lower categorical scores. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.36) faces a tough matchup against Manaea, we are keeping him in the UTIL spot to preserve his run-producing potential; however, owners should remain cautious of the volatility in the lower half of our order, as **Jackson Merrill** faces an elite arm in Imanaga, which could limit his output significantly today.",
